Subject: [202505] Restore virtual platform mapping before installer assembly

The sonic-device-data recipe generates the single-ASIC KVM platform_asic file
in the source tree. Restoring its cached Debian package skips this side effect.
The resulting installer omits x86_64-kvm_x86_64-r0 from platforms_asic, so ONIE
rejects the VS installer and install_sonic.py times out after repeated attempts.

Regenerate the file before collecting installer platforms, using exactly the
VS/VPP selection in src/sonic-device-data/Makefile. Keep platform filtering and
the installer's ASIC compatibility check intact; do not force installation or
disable package caching.

Origin of dynamic generation: https://github.com/sonic-net/sonic-buildimage/pull/21188
Failure: https://github.com/ITJamie/sonic-vs-builder/actions/runs/42711418118
Tested against sonic-buildimage ff3c0c9f686a1d0dbddbe813b233b3b7a51bd8e2.
Remove when upstream generates installer platform mappings independently of
whether sonic-device-data is built or restored from cache.

--- a/build_image.sh
+++ b/build_image.sh
@@ -101,6 +101,14 @@
 generate_device_list()
 {
     local platforms_asic=$1
+
+    # A cached sonic-device-data package skips its source-tree side effect.
+    # Match src/sonic-device-data/Makefile before collecting installer platforms.
+    if [ "$CONFIGURED_PLATFORM" = "vpp" ]; then
+        echo "vpp" > ./device/virtual/x86_64-kvm_x86_64-r0/platform_asic
+    else
+        echo "vs" > ./device/virtual/x86_64-kvm_x86_64-r0/platform_asic
+    fi
 
     # Create an empty function, and later append to it
     echo -n > $platforms_asic
